    "created_at": "2024-10-14T17:10:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-10-14T17:14:22Z",
    "body": "https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=20003 was closed in favor of this bug.  There is an outstanding issue in that golang's net/http library implements this spec exactly.  \r\nhttps://github.com/golang/go/issues/47492, etc\r\n\r\nThe function DetectContentType() returns of that package returns `text/plain; charset=utf-8,`. if you feed in the first 512 bytes of an SVG, because this spec doesn't support image/svg+xml.  The golang maintainers will not implement anything that is not in this spec. \r\n\r\nSo there are two fixes.\r\n\r\n1)Amend this spec.\r\n2) tell the golang maintainers they should not implement this spec (this spec is for browsers and only for files NOT received via HTTP) and make a new spec that does include image/svg+xml so they can implement that one instead.  \r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
